>


Only someone who doesn't care about the on-going proliferation of the
language would say something like this. Knowing how the grammar works in a
general way and being able to 'cope' with an actually cumbersome gimste are
completely different qualities a beginner should possess but I'm certainly
not going to advocate for the latter. In fact, we're going to try to
improve that situation.



>
>  That way it becomes much easier to get related gismu to align.
>>>>
>>>
>>> All gismu are "related".
>>>
